  "answer": "### Short Answer\nYes, today is the last day to file the annual income tax return of an individual, which is due on or before the fifteenth (15th) day of April of each year.\n\n### Controlling Authorities\nThis requirement is established under Section 51(C)(1) of the National Internal Revenue Code (NIRC), which states that the return of any individual shall be filed on or before April 15 of each year covering income for the preceding taxable year.\n\n### Interpretation\nThe NIRC mandates that individual taxpayers must submit their income tax returns by April 15. This deadline applies to all individuals required to file, including citizens and resident aliens, and is crucial for compliance with tax obligations.\n\n### Practical Meaning\nTaxpayers should ensure that their returns are filed by the deadline to avoid penalties and interest for late filing. It is advisable to prepare and submit the return well in advance of the deadline to account for any potential issues that may arise during the filing process.",
